51 AM Third message! 12:00:57 AM Message from page 1! 12:01:04 AM\n- textbox \"Type a message...\"\n- button \"Send\"<|\"|>}<tool_response|><|channel>thought\nIt appeared in `page-2` as well! SSE is working.\n\nI have completed all the tasks.\n\nLet me double check the requirements.\n\n1. Project Initialization:\n- [x] 1.1 Initialize the Node.js project and install backend dependencies (express, @electric-sql/pglite, cors)\n- [x] 1.2 Initialize the Vanilla JS / Vite project for the frontend and install frontend dependencies\n- [x] 1.3 Set up basic npm scripts for concurrently running backend and frontend development servers\n- [x] 1.4 Make the app start from a fresh checkout with no manual steps: once the dependencies declared in its package.json files are installed, `npm run dev` at the project root starts both the backend and the frontend, the backend creates any directory it needs (such as PGLite's data directory), and the page the frontend serves reaches the backend's API and event stream\n\n2. Backend Infrastructure & Database:\n- [x] 2.1 Set up a basic Express server with CORS and JSON body parsing\n- [x] 2.2 Initialize embedded PGLite configured to write to the local file system\n- [x] 2.3 Create the database initialization script (create `messages` table with `id`, `text`, `created_at`)\n- [x] 2.4 Create the historical messages endpoint (`GET /api/messages`) to fetch initial state\n\n3. Real-time Capabilities (SSE):\n- [x] 3.1 Implement the SSE endpoint (`GET /api/stream`) that maintains active connections with clients\n- [x] 3.2 Implement the messaging endpoint (`POST /api/messages`) to insert text into PGLite\n- [x] 3.3 Broadcast new messages to all active SSE connections when a new message is successfully inserted\n\n4. Frontend Implementation:\n- [x] 4.1 Create the basic HTML layout containing a message list and a text input form\n- [x] 4.2 Fetch the message history (`GET /api/messages`) on initial page load and render messages\n- [x] 4.3 Connect to the SSE endpoint (`GET /api/stream`) using `EventSource` to listen for new messages\n- [x] 4.4 Append incoming real-time messages to the DOM seamlessly\n- [x] 4.5 Wire up the form submission to send a `POST` request to `/api/messages` and clear the input\n\nEverything seems to be done.\n\nI'll just do a quick cleanup: remove the check script.\n\n<channel|><|tool_call>call:run_command{command:<|\"|>rm backend/check_pglite.js<|\"|>}<tool_call|><|tool_response>response:run_command{value:<|\"|>$ rm backend/check_pglite.js\n[exit 0]\n<|\"|>}<tool_response|><|channel>thought\n","generated":""}
